ut Allen's running to the  next unit but Nestor essentially took  over all of that well I mean there was  no given the time we didn't have a  choice yeah we had to we had to sort of  divide and conquer it at some point so  so my storyline was somewhat contained  with with swen so I we could do that but  this man was running not no joke between  three sets it went yeah it was insane uh  one of the things I personally anytime  I've worn 80s clothing it makes me crazy  I hate it and I'm just curious what it  was like for you and for everyone else  because 80s clothing is terrible  especially in Georgia humidity yeah and  that yeah that leather jacket didn't it  wasn't very forgiving and the dead heat  of Georgia and Thomasville and Valdosta  you know that was and the humidity was  lovely  um yeah the sweaters are great you know  Josh's flannel sweaters oh those are I  know I saw that in the trailers like I  forgot about that sweater amazing yeah  the 80s man the Merry-Go-Round sweaters  those those are the days  um but I had the best laugh my wardrobe  fitting was the first meeting I had  after actually even before I met you it  was wardrobe and just going oh my God  this has taken me way back it's a good  reason we got rid of these clothes but  uh I I gotta tell you it was fun  whenever you get to wear something like  that as an actor already you're you've  it's almost like it's a gift to an actor  because you're already developing a  character you know it's almost like a  stage actor the first thing they want to  wear is a character's shoes to see see  how they walk you know and it's it's no  different with clothing one of the  things about this film is you can't  believe it's true you know most bank  robbers are lucky to rob a few Banks  once you crack 50 it's it's just such  it's Preposterous but yet it's true can  you sort of talk about that aspect of  the story yeah well the sheer volume I  mean that's what hooked me right from  the get-go because I'd heard the moniker  flying Bandit but I didn't know the  extent to which he had actually pulled  off all of these crimes and the way the  flare and the panat like how he did all  of that it sucked me right in and I knew  that after reading the book I was nobody  is gonna like when we screen to First  Cut someone said he just paid a homeless  guy for his health card that would never  happen I'm like right no it happened and  so that's why we ended up putting those  sort of captions on screen because  people would be like taken out of the  film there's no way this actually  happened all of it did even the pizza  ordering the pizza at the police station  after being arrested it was it was  insane is there anything you want to ask  yeah truth is Stranger Than Fiction it  really is but you're right I'm so glad  you did put those things not only are  they funny but but you're right you  would question that um I yeah that was  that's part of the joy the part of the  ride of this they said it is so  unbelievable and yet it isn't it it  actually happened and and few few of  these films are getting made these these  incredibly uh beautiful character-driven  true stories you know uh that have  elements of action and credit to you  brother and the investors to take a  chance on this one uh last question an  individual for each of you um what's  going on with this driver TV series is  that is that happening I'm waiting on  the studio to call me after I did  Uncharted I was very blessed to be in a  position to get the rights to a lot of  video games people trusted mean sort of  what I pulled off with Fillion and you  know everything is sort of an initiative  these days all the studios you know turn  around development how I'm always  waiting on a call so I'm ready to go I'm  also very curious about Shogun  um oh yeah yeah and so what can you  tease about that because the project  seems very cool it's an incredible  project we shot at in Vancouver you know  uh which doubled for for Japan and 